blessed +3 Tsurugi of Muramasa
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
vs. small monster       vs. large monster       vs. major demon
1-16 (tsurugi)          3-20                    3-20
                                                4-24 (bl. vs. und.)
4-19 (+3)               6-23                    7-27
     (artifact?)
11.5 (average)          14.5                    17

The Tsurugi of Muramasa has a 10% chance for instant kill by bisecting the
monster if it is small. If the monster is large the Tsurugi can "slice
deep" and hence do 50-60 points of extra damage.
Only lawfuls or samurais can wield The Tsurugi. Tsurugi is a two-handed
weapon. Lawful.


blessed +3 Staff of Aesculapius
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
vs. small monster       vs. large monster       vs. major demon
1-6  (quaterstaff)      1-6                     1-6
                                                2-10 (bl. vs. und.)
4-9  (+3)               4-9                     5-13
     (artifact?)
7.5  (average)          7.5                     9

The Staff of Aesculapius drains life from the opponent. It regenerates
the wielder. When invoked it also heals. Only neutrals or healers can
wield The Staff. Neutral.


blessed +3 Sceptre of Might
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
vs. small monster       vs. large monster       vs. major demon
1-6  (quaterstaff)      1-6                     1-6
                                                2-10 (bl. vs. und.)
4-9  (+3)               4-9                     5-13
     (artifact?)
7.5   (average)         7.5                     9

The Sceptre of Might does special damage against non-aligned monsters
(about 20-30 points). When invoked causes conflict.
Only lawfuls or cave(wo)men can wield The Sceptre. Lawful.

The practical maximum of enchantment is +7 in 3.1.x.

